    "All five complete runs received exactly 23 chunks and emitted four generations in strict order [1,2,3,4] at cumulative source byte counts [32768,65536,81920,163840].",
    "CADisplayLink first observed a preview at median 129144833 ns and final pixels at median 812619167 ns from per-test trace origin.",
    "The median observed progressive-visible window was 683474334 ns; this is descriptive Simulator evidence, not physical presentation latency.",
    "Across five identity replacements, publication fence to old-preview suppression had median 138125 ns and oldPreviewObservedAfterReplacementCount was zero.",
    "Repeated execution exposed and corrected a test-oracle defect: process-local CGImage pointer addresses can be reused after deallocation, so trace correlation now strongly retains participating images and strips pointer tokens before evidence serialization."
